.Dd November 18, 2026
.Dt EXFAT_FAULTGEN 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm exfat_faultgen
.Nd exFAT file system fault injection and stress-testing utility
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl h | Fl Fl help
.Op Fl j | Fl Fl json
.Op Fl n | Fl Fl dry-run
.Op Fl v | Fl Fl verbose
.Ar option
.Ar image
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility inspects exFAT file systems and injects targeted, specification-level
corruptions into an exFAT file system image or block device.
It is primarily designed to verify consistency checking and recovery
routines in
.Xr fsck_exfat 8
and kernel drivers such as
.Xr mount_exfat 8 .
.Pp
Exactly one fault injection or utility option must be specified per invocation.
Mutations directly alter on-disk structures while maintaining partition
geometry unless a fault specifically targets geometric properties.
Inspection and utility options operate in read-only mode and do not modify
the image.
.Sh OPTIONS
The following general options are available:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl h , Fl Fl help
Display a synopsis of available command-line options and exit.
.It Fl j , Fl Fl json
Emit inspection and verification results in machine-readable JSON format.
Can be combined with
.Fl Fl verify
or any of the
.Fl Fl dump-*
options.
When specified without an explicit utility option, defaults to
.Fl Fl verify .
.It Fl n , Fl Fl dry-run
Simulate the fault injection without writing mutations to disk.
When combined with
.Fl v ,
diagnostic messages show the exact offsets and values that would be
modified.
.It Fl v , Fl Fl verbose
Enable verbose diagnostic output, printing opened image geometry,
cluster sizes, and sector offsets.
.El
.Pp
The following inspection and utility options are available:
.Ss Inspection and Utility Options
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl Fl dump-all
Perform a comprehensive audit of the exFAT volume, combining all inspection
utilities into a single unified report.
Displays Boot Sector parameters and verifies checksums (Spec Section 3),
inspects the File Allocation Table and cluster chains (Spec Section 4.1),
evaluates Allocation Bitmap status and runs (Spec Section 7.1),
and recursively audits all directory entry sets, stream extensions, and
file names while detecting anomalies or cycles (Spec Section 6, 7).
Inspection runs in read-only mode and does not modify the image.
.It Fl Fl dump-bitmap Op Ar range
Inspect and display cluster allocation status from the Allocation Bitmap
(Spec Section 7.1).
When invoked without arguments, displays the full allocation run map and
summary statistics for all clusters in the volume.
If
.Ar range
is given as a single cluster number
.Pq e.g., Ar 5 ,
the allocation state of that cluster is queried.
If
.Ar range
is specified as a cluster span
.Pq e.g., Ar 2,100 No or Ar 2-100 ,
allocation runs and statistics are restricted to the given range.
Inspection runs in read-only mode and does not modify the image.
.It Fl Fl dump-boot Op Ar region
Inspect and display Boot Sector and Volume Boot Record (VBR) parameters,
compare Main and Backup boot sectors, and verify 32-bit boot region
checksums (Spec Section 3.1, 3.4).
When invoked without arguments, displays the Main Boot Sector fields,
compares Main and Backup boot sectors for discrepancies, and verifies
both Main and Backup region checksums.
If
.Ar region
is specified as
.Cm main ,
only the Main Boot Sector and its checksum are displayed.
If specified as
.Cm backup ,
the Backup Boot Sector (Sector 12) and its checksum are displayed.
Inspection runs in read-only mode and does not modify the image.
.It Fl Fl dump-fat Op Ar range | cn
Inspect and display File Allocation Table (FAT) entries, trace cluster
chains, detect circular references, compare dual-FAT mirrors on TexFAT
volumes, and report allocation statistics (Spec Section 4.1).
When invoked without arguments, displays the entire cluster heap allocation
runs and overall FAT statistics.
If specified as a single cluster number
.Pq e.g., Ar 5 ,
displays the 32-bit FAT entry value, entry classification (Free, EOF,
Bad Cluster, or Next Cluster), sector and byte offsets within the FAT,
comparison against mirror FAT (if dual-FAT), and traces the cluster chain
forward with cycle detection.
If specified as a cluster span
.Pq e.g., Ar 2,100 No or Ar 2-100 ,
allocation runs, bad cluster markers, EOF markers, and statistics are
restricted to the given range.
Inspection runs in read-only mode and does not modify the image.
.It Fl Fl dump-dentries Op Ar path | cn
Inspect and display exFAT directory entries, directory entry sets, stream
extensions, file names, attributes, timestamps, and verify SetChecksum and
NameHash integrity across the volume (Spec Section 6.3, 7.4).
When invoked without arguments, displays all directory entries starting from
the Root Directory and recursively traverses subdirectories while detecting
circular directory loops.
If specified as a cluster number
.Pq e.g., Ar 5 ,
restricts inspection to the directory starting at that cluster.
If specified as a path or file name
.Pq e.g., Ar /docs No or Ar sample.txt ,
inspects the matching directory or displays the detailed directory entry set
of the target file.
Validates 16-bit SetChecksum, NameHash, missing Stream Extension entries,
NameLength field consistency, FirstCluster heap bounds, directory stream
allocation constraints, ValidDataLength versus DataLength, NoFatChain
continuity, and flags invalid characters, orphaned secondary entries, or
directory recursion loops.
Inspection runs in read-only mode and does not modify the image.
.It Fl Fl verify
Perform a non-destructive volume consistency verification, aggregating defect
counters across the Boot Region, File Allocation Table, Allocation Bitmap,
and Directory Entry sets.
Exits with status 0 if the volume is clean, or status 1 if any corruptions
or specification violations are detected.
Inspection runs in read-only mode and does not modify the image.
.El
.Pp
The following fault injection options are available:
.Ss Boot and VBR Options (Spec Section 3.1)
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl Fl boot-checksum-mismatch
Invert the 32-bit checksum in Sector 11 of the Main Boot region
(Spec Section 3.4).
.It Fl Fl boot-backup-mismatch
Mutate the volume serial number in the Main Boot Sector without updating
the Backup Boot Sector (Spec Section 3.1).
.It Fl Fl boot-flags-reserved Op Ar mask
Set invalid reserved bits (bits 4\(en15) in the
.Va VolumeFlags
field of the Main Boot Sector (Spec Section 3.1.13), defaulting to 0x0010.
.It Fl Fl boot-percent-in-use Op Ar val
Set the
.Va PercentInUse
field to an invalid value (>100 and != 0xFF), defaulting to 150
(Spec Section 3.1.18).
.It Fl Fl boot-drive-select Op Ar val
Set the
.Va DriveSelect
field to an invalid INT 13h drive number (!= 0x00 and != 0x80),
defaulting to 0x01 (Spec Section 3.1.17).
.It Fl Fl boot-zero-fields
Inject non-zero pattern bytes into the reserved
.Va bs_must_be_zero
and
.Va bs_reserved
fields (Spec Section 3.1, 3.1.3).
.El
.Ss File Allocation Table (FAT) Options (Spec Section 4.1)
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl Fl fat-cycle Ar cluster
Create a circular cluster cycle in the FAT chain (Spec Section 4.1.3).
If
.Ar cluster
is specified as
.Ar cn ,
the entry points back to itself.
If specified as
.Ar src,dst ,
entry
.Ar src
points to
.Ar dst .
.It Fl Fl fat-bad-cluster Ar cluster
Mark the specified allocated cluster as
.Dv EXFAT_FAT_BAD
(0xFFFFFFF7) in the FAT (Spec Section 4.1.3).
.It Fl Fl fat-crosslink Ar src,dst
Cross-link two distinct cluster chains by setting the FAT entry for
cluster
.Ar src
to point to cluster
.Ar dst
(Spec Section 4.1.3).
.It Fl Fl fat-out-of-bounds Ar cluster
Point the FAT entry of the specified cluster beyond the valid cluster
heap range (>= ClusterCount + 2 and < 0xFFFFFFF7) (Spec Section 4.1.3).
An explicit out-of-bounds cluster target can optionally be passed as
.Ar cn,target .
.It Fl Fl fat-mirror-diverge Op Ar cluster
Mutate an entry in the secondary FAT on TexFAT volumes
.Pq NumberOfFats == 2
to cause divergence from the active FAT (Spec Section 3.1.13.1, 4.1).
Returns an error if the volume only has a single FAT.
.El
.Ss Allocation Bitmap Options (Spec Section 7.1)
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl Fl bitmap-orphan Ar cluster
Mark an unreferenced, free cluster as allocated in the Allocation Bitmap
(Spec Section 7.1).
.It Fl Fl bitmap-false-free Ar cluster
Clear the allocation bitmap bit for an allocated cluster, making it
falsely appear free while still referenced by a file (Spec Section 7.1).
.It Fl Fl bitmap-truncate
Truncate the recorded
.Va DataLength
in the Allocation Bitmap directory entry to less than the required
cluster heap coverage (Spec Section 7.1.4).
.It Fl Fl bitmap-mirror-diverge Op Ar cluster
Mutate the allocation bit of a cluster in the secondary Allocation Bitmap
on dual-FAT volumes
.Pq NumberOfFats == 2
to cause divergence from the active Allocation Bitmap
(Spec Section 3.1.13.1, 7.1).
Returns an error if the volume only has a single FAT.
.It Fl Fl bitmap-flags-reserved Op Ar flags
Set invalid reserved bits in the
.Va BitmapFlags
field of the Allocation Bitmap directory entry (Spec Section 7.1.2).
On single-FAT volumes without arguments, sets
.Dv EXFAT_BITMAP_FLAG_SECOND
and reserved bit 7.
.El
.Ss Directory Entry and Stream Options (Spec Section 6.3, 7.4, 7.6, 7.7)
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl Fl dentry-checksum Ar target
Corrupt the 16-bit
.Va SetChecksum
field in the primary File Directory Entry (0x85) of
.Ar target
(Spec Section 6.3.3, 7.4.3).
.Ar target
may be specified by filename, entry index, or starting cluster.
.It Fl Fl dentry-secondary-count Ar target Op Ar count
Corrupt the 8-bit
.Va SecondaryCount
field in the primary File Directory Entry (0x85) of
.Ar target
(Spec Section 7.4.2).
If
.Ar count
is provided, sets the field to that value; otherwise sets it to 1 (violating the
minimum count of 2) or decrements the count, while recalculating
.Va SetChecksum
to isolate the structural count defect.
.It Fl Fl dentry-name-hash Ar target Op Ar hash
Corrupt the 16-bit
.Va NameHash
field in the Stream Extension entry (0xC0) of
.Ar target
(Spec Section 7.6.4).
If
.Ar hash
is provided, sets the field to that value; otherwise inverts the stored hash,
while recalculating
.Va SetChecksum
to isolate the name hash mismatch.
.It Fl Fl dentry-invalid-name-chars Ar target Op Ar char
Inject forbidden characters into the File Name secondary entries (0xC1) of
.Ar target
(Spec Section 7.7.3).
If
.Ar char
is provided, injects that character code; otherwise injects a colon
.Pq Ql \&: ,
while recalculating
.Va SetChecksum
to isolate the invalid character defect.
.It Fl Fl dentry-size-mismatch Ar target Op Ar bytes
Modify the
.Va DataLength
and
.Va ValidDataLength
fields in the Stream Extension entry (0xC0) of
.Ar target
to create a discrepancy with the allocated cluster chain in the FAT (Spec
Section 7.6.5, 7.6.7).
If
.Ar bytes
is provided, sets both lengths to that value; otherwise sets them to exceed
the allocated FAT chain by two clusters, while recalculating
.Va SetChecksum .
.It Fl Fl stream-vdl-exceeds-dl Ar target
Set the
.Va ValidDataLength
field to exceed
.Va DataLength
in the Stream Extension entry (0xC0) of
.Ar target ,
recalculating
.Va SetChecksum
to isolate the VDL violation (Spec Section 7.6.5).
.It Fl Fl stream-nofatchain-fragment Ar target
Assert the
.Dv EXFAT_FLAG_NO_FAT_CHAIN
flag on the stream extension of
.Ar target
while fragmenting its cluster allocation in the FAT (Spec Section 6.4.2, 7.6.2).
.It Fl Fl dentry-orphaned-secondary Op Ar offset
Write an unparented secondary Stream Extension entry (0xC0) at the
specified directory slot or byte offset
.Ar offset
without a preceding primary entry (Spec Section 6.3, 6.4).
.It Fl Fl dentry-root-in-subdir Ar target
Set the
.Va FirstCluster
of directory
.Ar target
to point back to the Root Directory cluster, creating an invalid directory
loop (Spec Section 6.3).
.El
.Ss Up-case Table Options (Spec Section 7.2)
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl Fl upcase-checksum-mismatch Op Ar csum
Corrupt the 32-bit
.Va TableChecksum
field in the Up-case Table directory entry (0x82) in the Root Directory
(Spec Section 7.2.2).
If
.Ar csum
is provided, sets the checksum to that value; otherwise inverts the stored
checksum bits.
.It Fl Fl upcase-truncate Op Ar bytes | chain
Truncate the recorded
.Va DataLength
field or the FAT cluster chain of the Up-case Table directory entry (0x82)
(Spec Section 7.2.4).
If
.Ar chain
is given, terminates the FAT allocation chain at the first cluster while
retaining DataLength.
If
.Ar bytes
is given, sets DataLength to that byte count.
When omitted, truncates DataLength so the compressed Up-case Table stream cannot
define all 65,536 characters and terminates the FAT allocation chain.
.El
.Ss Volume Label and GUID Options (Spec Section 7.3, 7.5)
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl Fl label-duplicate Op Ar name
Inject a duplicate Volume Label directory entry (0x83) into the Root Directory
(Spec Section 7.3.1).
If
.Ar name
is provided, assigns that label to the duplicate entry.
.It Fl Fl label-invalid-chars Op Ar char
Inject forbidden characters
.Pq Ql \&" , Ql * , Ql / , Ql \&: , Ql < , Ql > , Ql \&? , Ql \e , Ql \&|
or control characters below 0x0020
into the Volume Label directory entry (Spec Section 7.3.3).
.It Fl Fl label-length Op Ar count
Set
.Va CharacterCount
to exceed the specification limit of 11 characters (e.g. 12) in the Volume Label
directory entry (Spec Section 7.3.2).
.It Fl Fl guid-duplicate Op Ar guid
Inject a duplicate Volume GUID directory entry (0xA0) into the Root Directory
(Spec Section 7.5.1).
If
.Ar guid
is provided in standard GUID format, assigns that identifier to the
duplicate entry.
.It Fl Fl guid-invalid Op Ar field
Set non-zero
.Va SecondaryCount
(Spec Section 7.5.2) or non-zero
.Va GeneralPrimaryFlags
(Spec Section 7.5.4) in the Volume GUID directory entry.
If
.Ar field
is
.Cm flags ,
mutates GeneralPrimaryFlags; if
.Cm count ,
mutates SecondaryCount; otherwise mutates both.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Perform non-destructive volume consistency verification:
.Pp
.Dl "exfat_faultgen --verify exfat.img"
.Pp
Emit volume verification in JSON format for automated test runners:
.Pp
.Dl "exfat_faultgen --json exfat.img"
.Pp
Perform a comprehensive volume audit and inspection report:
.Pp
.Dl "exfat_faultgen --dump-all exfat.img"
.Pp
Dump Boot Sector parameters and verify checksums:
.Pp
.Dl "exfat_faultgen --dump-boot exfat.img"
.Pp
Inspect only the Backup Boot Sector:
.Pp
.Dl "exfat_faultgen --dump-boot backup exfat.img"
.Pp
Inspect allocation status for cluster 10:
.Pp
.Dl "exfat_faultgen --dump-bitmap 10 exfat.img"
.Pp
Display allocation runs across clusters 2 through 100:
.Pp
.Dl "exfat_faultgen --dump-bitmap 2,100 exfat.img"
.Pp
Dump full volume allocation statistics:
.Pp
.Dl "exfat_faultgen --dump-bitmap exfat.img"
.Pp
Inspect FAT entry and trace cluster chain for cluster 5:
.Pp
.Dl "exfat_faultgen --dump-fat 5 exfat.img"
.Pp
Display FAT allocation runs across clusters 2 through 100:
.Pp
.Dl "exfat_faultgen --dump-fat 2,100 exfat.img"
.Pp
Dump full volume FAT statistics and allocation runs:
.Pp
.Dl "exfat_faultgen --dump-fat exfat.img"
.Pp
Dump all directory entries across the volume:
.Pp
.Dl "exfat_faultgen --dump-dentries exfat.img"
.Pp
Inspect directory entries in a specific subdirectory:
.Pp
.Dl "exfat_faultgen --dump-dentries /docs exfat.img"
.Pp
Inspect directory entry set for a specific file:
.Pp
.Dl "exfat_faultgen --dump-dentries sample.txt exfat.img"
.Pp
Inject a boot region checksum mismatch into an image:
.Pp
.Dl "exfat_faultgen --boot-checksum-mismatch exfat.img"
.Pp
Simulate creating a circular FAT loop on cluster 5 in dry-run verbose mode:
.Pp
.Dl "exfat_faultgen -n -v --fat-cycle 5 exfat.img"
.Pp
Mark cluster 12 as a bad cluster:
.Pp
.Dl "exfat_faultgen --fat-bad-cluster 12 exfat.img"
.Pp
Corrupt the Up-case Table checksum:
.Pp
.Dl "exfat_faultgen --upcase-checksum-mismatch exfat.img"
.Pp
Truncate the Up-case Table data length:
.Pp
.Dl "exfat_faultgen --upcase-truncate exfat.img"
.Pp
Set ValidDataLength greater than DataLength on file
.Dq test.txt :
.Pp
.Dl "exfat_faultgen --stream-vdl-exceeds-dl test.txt exfat.img"
.Pp
Corrupt SecondaryCount on file
.Dq test.txt :
.Pp
.Dl "exfat_faultgen --dentry-secondary-count test.txt exfat.img"
.Pp
Inject an invalid character into the name of file
.Dq test.txt :
.Pp
.Dl "exfat_faultgen --dentry-invalid-name-chars test.txt exfat.img"
.Pp
Verify repair capabilities with
.Xr fsck_exfat 8 :
.Pp
.Dl "exfat_faultgen --bitmap-orphan 8 exfat.img"
.Dl "fsck_exfat -y exfat.img"
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr fsck_exfat 8 ,
.Xr mount_exfat 8 ,
.Xr newfs_exfat 8
.Sh STANDARDS
The exFAT disk layout, structures, and fault injection criteria conform to the
.Rs
.%A Microsoft Corporation
.%T exFAT File System Specification
.%I Microsoft Learn
.%U https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/fileio/exfat-specification
.Re
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
utility was developed for FreeBSD to support automated file system
consistency validation and repair testing.
